    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure requirement for membership level 4 in `MembershipLevelCalculator` (`src/main/java/.../util/MembershipLevelCalculator.java`).\n\n**The change:**\n- Split the old single cap (`MAX_LEVEL = 3`) into two constants: `PRE_TENURE_MAX_LEVEL = 3` (the ceiling for the email + no-namesake factors) and `MAX_LEVEL = 4` (the overall ceiling, reachable only via tenure).\n- Added `TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS = 365`.\n- After capping the pre-tenure factors at 3, the calculator now awards one more point when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days, up to level 4.\n- Tenure is computed by a small private `hasQualifyingTenure` helper: `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`, treating a null registration date as zero tenure.\n\n**Why this satisfies the spec:**\n- A newly created owner has `registrationDate == today` (set to `LocalDate.now()` on create), so tenure is 0 \u2192 no tenure point \u2192 never exceeds level 3.\n- A new owner with an email, `namesakeCount == 0`, and a 3-member household computes `1 (base) + 1 (email) + 1 (no namesake) = 3`, then no tenure point \u2192 level 3, matching the acceptance test (`membershipLevel == 3`).\n\nI kept the logic in the existing calculator (its single responsibility), reused `LocalDate.now()` / `ChronoUnit` in the same idiom the rest of the codebase uses (e.g. `PetAgeValidator`, `AgeBandResolver`), and made no changes to the mapper or model since they already delegate correctly. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).",
